  "summary": {
    "bill_id": "sjres-119-18",
    "short_summary": "This joint resolution nullifies a Consumer Financial Protection Bureau rule regulating overdraft credit and fees at very large financial institutions, ensuring the rule has no force or effect.",
    "long_summary": "This joint resolution provides that Congress disapproves the final rule submitted by the Bureau of Consumer Financial Protection (CFPB) titled \"Overdraft Lending: Very Large Financial Institutions,\" which was published in the Federal Register on December 30, 2024.\n\nUnder the resolution, the rule shall have no force or effect. The CFPB's rule had amended Regulations E and Z to modify regulatory exemptions for overdraft credit offered by very large financial institutions. According to the agency, the rule was intended to require these overdraft extensions to adhere to consumer protections applicable to other credit products unless the institution limited fees to recovering estimated costs and losses.",
    "who_it_affects": "This resolution directly affects the Bureau of Consumer Financial Protection by voiding its rule, as well as very large financial institutions that would have been subject to the rule's requirements and restrictions regarding overdraft lending and fees.",
